            "bug_id": 19194,
            "text": "Since r90200, read.dcf() with the default all = FALSE no longer matches\na repeated field whose name contains invalid UTF-8: each repeat adds\nanother column with the same name.\n\nReproducible example:\n\n    x <- strrep(\"e\\xfe: v\\n\\n\", 5)\n    con <- textConnection(x)\n    r <- read.dcf(con)\n    close(con)\n    dim(r)\n    ## [1] 5 5\n    colnames(r)\n    ## [1] \"e<fe>\" \"e<fe>\" \"e<fe>\" \"e<fe>\" \"e<fe>\"\n\nExpected: 5 x 1, as read.dcf(all = TRUE) and R 4.6.1 give. Because each\nnew column copies the whole matrix, 2000 records take 94 seconds\n(trunk r90590, release build; 0.002 seconds with the patch).\n\nAnalysis: do_readDCF() in src/main/dcf.c stores a new field name via\nmkCharUTF8sub(), which repairs invalid bytes as \"<xx>\", but compares\nlater lines with the stored names on their raw bytes, so \"e\\xfe\" never\nmatches \"e<fe>\". The all = TRUE code repairs each line before matching.\n\nProposed patch: attached as read-dcf-invalid-utf8-field-names.diff\n(against r90605). It repairs each invalid line with reEnc3() as soon as\nit is read, as the all = TRUE code does, and guards the two\nline[20] = '\\0' truncations in the error paths, since the repaired copy\ncan be shorter than 21 bytes. It adds a regression test, and make\ntest-Reg passes. It applies independently of the patch in bug 19183.\n\nFound by the read.dcf() fuzz target in\nhttps://github.com/r-devel/r-oss-fuzz. The patch is also submitted as\nhttps://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/349, where CI results can be seen.",
